From dce3130011493566d59dac85e1640ae5ce83d00b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EberhartLeberhart <EberhartLeberhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:57:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 58/59] ASoC: sprd: pcm-dma: prepare a new DMA descriptor after
 stop

The DMA descriptor is prepared once in hw_params() and submitted on
every TRIGGER_START. TRIGGER_STOP calls dmaengine_terminate_async(),
and the Spreadtrum DMA driver frees all descriptors of the channel at
that point, including the submitted one.

When the stream is restarted without a new hw_params() call (prepare
followed by start, as PipeWire does after an xrun or when a node is
resumed), the freed descriptor is submitted again. vchan_tx_submit()
then moves a list node that was already removed and poisoned, or
writes into memory that has been reused by someone else:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address dead000000000108
  pc : vchan_tx_submit+0x58/0x8c
  Call trace:
   vchan_tx_submit+0x58/0x8c
   sprd_pcm_trigger+0x68/0x204 [snd_soc_sprd_platform]
   snd_soc_pcm_component_trigger+0x168/0x224 [snd_soc_core]
   ...

Earlier crashes of the same kind showed up as slab corruption in
kfree() from unrelated tasks.

Move the descriptor preparation into a helper. Call it from hw_params()
as before and from a new prepare() callback for every channel whose
descriptor was consumed by TRIGGER_STOP. Clear the descriptor pointer
on stop and when the channels are released, so a stale pointer is never
submitted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W8YQkFAqgbw689knydrHtG
